  "abilities": [],
  "behavior": "It is highly aggressive and has a strong tendency to burrow during combat to reposition and attack from underground. Its moves resemble those of the Northern Scorpion, but the timings and patterns are not exactly the same.",
  "interactionWithPlayer": "It can easily mislead players who are used to fighting the Northern Scorpion. Some attacks look familiar, but reacting with exactly the same block timings can lead to unexpected hits.",
  "interactionWithCreatures": "It often shares its territory with scorplings and juvenile scorpions, as well as mosquitoes, wasps, and other creatures. Because the area is crowded with wildlife, it is common to find it already fighting other insects, which may significantly reduce its health.",
  "strategy": "Use Busting damage and do not rely too heavily on Northern Scorpion timings. A charged or critical attack can interrupt its attempt to burrow. Before entering the fight, watch the surroundings: if it is already fighting other creatures, let them weaken each other and step in once the scorpion is injured or ready to be finished off.",
